September-24-2026.html#thm:blowup","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:afc50c3765f044d894cf2caa10f5df4eaba23624f6357ca62e93a75964e1e817","file":"preprints/Stable-Self-Similar-Blowup-for-a-Supercritical-Defocusing-Schrodinger-Equation-on-the-Torus-September-24-2026/build/main.tex","line":67,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"44fbe763d2429a3d5bce9038a5428014ee825594139005f3efcf5a1b824ad4d6","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Stable-Self-Similar-Blowup-for-a-Supercritical-Defocusing-Schrodinger-Equation-on-the-Torus-September-24-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:afc50c3765f044d894cf2caa10f5df4eaba23624f6357ca62e93a75964e1e817","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Stable-Self-Similar-Blowup-for-a-Supercritical-Defocusing-Schrodinger-Equation-on-the-Torus-September-24-2026/build/main.tex#L67"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:blowup}\nThere exist an odd integer $p\\geq3$, a finite integer $k>8$, and a\nnonempty open set $\\mathcal U\\subset H^k(\\mathbb T^{12};\\mathbb C)$\nwith the following property. For every $u_0\\in\\mathcal U$, the unique\nlocal solution of \\eqref{eq:nls} extends to\n\\[\n u\\in C([0,T);H^k)\\cap C^1([0,T);H^{k-2})\n\\]\nfor some finite $T>0$, but has no continuous $H^k$ extension through $T$.\nMore precisely, there are $x_*\\in\\mathbb T^{12}$ and $c_0>0$ such that\n\\[\n \\lim_{t\\uparrow T}(T-t)^{1/(p-1)}|u(t,x_*)|=c_0.\n\\]\nThe power can be chosen sufficiently large, and $k$ is then fixed after\nthat choice."}
